      "environment_kind": "definition",
      "source_line_start": 25,
      "source_line_end": 43,
      "current_tex": "\\begin{definition}[Supremum]\n\\label{def:supremum}\nLet $(S,\\leq)$ be a partially ordered set, let $A\\subseteq S$, and let\n$s\\in S$. The element $s$ is the \\emph{supremum} of $A$, written\n$s=\\sup A$, if\n\\[\n  (\\forall a\\in A)(a\\leq s)\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n  (\\forall u\\in S)\n  \\left[\n    (\\forall a\\in A)(a\\leq u)\n    \\Longrightarrow\n    s\\leq u\n  \\right].\n\\]\nThus, $s$ is the least upper bound of $A$ in $S$.\n\\end{definition}",
      "formalizations": []
    }
  },
